This skill (v3.0.0) was rewritten in 2026 to target Russian text. It is a hybrid of
two upstream MIT-licensed skills, both adapted and reworked:

  - blader/humanizer            (https://github.com/blader/humanizer)
                                methodology: pattern catalog + before/after examples
  - SergeNS-mne/humanizer-ru    (https://github.com/SergeNS-mne/humanizer-ru)
                                Russian phrase-pattern catalog (canceljarit, genitive
                                chains, «является», calques, RU typography), adapted

The pattern selection, the tire-as-connector rule (aligned with this project's own
copywriting principles, not the upstream glyph-swap rule), the false-positive and
"signs of human writing" sections, and this SKILL.md's structure are original work.
Removed from the humanizer-ru source: the voice-passport / .humanizer/voice.json
layer, genre presets, --rough deliberate-imperfection mechanics, and the
"perfect grammar as an AI tell" section — out of scope for commercial landing copy.

Both upstream projects and this adaptation are MIT-licensed.

